## To Reviewers

Maintenance for PHP 5.x
 
## Objective of this PR

To enable the earliest PHP 5.6 applications to run as is. More for quality maintenance and to demonstrate the strength of BEAR.Sunday's long-term operation than for practical purposes.

Also, We remove @deprecated `AppInjector` and replace with `Injector::getInstance()` from unit test.

## How to verify ofd project works

### 1.Creating a project in PHP 5.6

First create a project in PHP 5.6: Composer v2.2 running in PHP 5.6 as composer22

```
composer22 create-project bear/skeleton app
```

The skeleton entry file and bootstrap file are respectively as follows.

Entry files

```php
<?php

$context = PHP_SAPI === 'cli' ? 'cli-hal-api-app' : 'hal-api-app';
require __DIR__ . '/bootstrap.php';.
```

Bootstrap file

```php
use BEAR\Package\Bootstrap;.
use Doctrine\Common\Annotations\AnnotationRegistry;

load: {
    /* @var $loader \Composer\Autoload\ClassLoader */
    $loader = require dirname(__DIR__) . '/vendor/autoload.php';.
    AnnotationRegistry::registerLoader([$loader, 'loadClass']);
}

route: {
    $context = 'cli-app';
    $app = (new Bootstrap)->getApp(__NAMESPACE__, $context);.
    /* @var $app AbstractApp \BEAR\Sunday\Extension\Application\AbstractApp */
    $request = $app->router->match($GLOBALS, $_SERVER);
}

try {
    // resource request
    $page = $app->resource
        ->{$request->method}
        ->uri($request->path)
        ->withQuery($request->query)
        ->request();
    /* @var $page \BEARResourceRequest */

    // representation transfer
    $page()->transfer($app->responder, $_SERVER);
    exit(0);
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    $app->error->handle($e, $request)->transfer();
    exit(1);
}
```

## 2. Erasing require-dev

Packages in the `require-dev section are not blocked from installation in the latest version (currently PHP 8.3), once this section is erased.

## 3. composer update

Use composer update to bring bear/package up to date. In this state, run the following command to check that it works.

```
php bootstrap/web.php get /
```

